WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:05.250
A scientist can find mass with a balance
and temperature with a thermometer.

2
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:11.780
In 1789, Jeremy Bentham claimed that
right and wrong were rooted in nature too.

3
00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:16.760
Nature, he wrote, has placed
mankind under two sovereign masters:

4
00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:18.850
pain and pleasure.

5
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:24.600
So can you find goodness in the world, the
way a scientist finds mass or temperature?

6
00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:28.080
In this mission, you'll
ask what moral words mean,

7
00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:30.500
and what could ever make them true.

8
00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:36.600
Then you'll meet a famous test from 1903
that any definition of good must face.

9
00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:41.640
Your mission: find out whether goodness
can be pinned down as a natural fact.
